From: dst+@cs.cmu.edu (Dave Touretzky)
Newsgroups: alt.sex,alt.censorship,alt.comp.acad-freedom.talk,comp.org.eff.talk
Subject:  CMU Faculty Senate opposes bboard ban
Date: 10 Nov 1994 23:15:20 GMT
Message-ID: <39u9i8$95l@casaba.srv.cs.cmu.edu>

At the CMU Faculty Senate meeting tonight, a resolution was passed opposing
the administration's ban on 15 electronic bulletin boards containing
digitized images.  The ban went into effect this past Tuesday.  The text of
the resolution follows.

-- Dave Touretzky, Senior Research Scientist, Computer Science Department

================================================================

    RESOLUTION PASSED NOVEMBER 10, 1994 BY CMU FACULTY SENATE

Whereas, this University has a long and proud tradition of protecting
freedom of expression and intellectual inquiry,

The Faculty Senate requests that the Administration take no action to
restrict access to information, or to prevent individuals from obtaining
and distributing information via electronic networks, unless an advisory
committee, with appropriate representation of the campus community, and
after due consultation with recognized experts, finds that failure to take
action in specific, limited cases would place the University at imminent
and grave risk of legal liability,

And further requests that until this committee has issued its first report,
the policy in effect as of November 7, 1994, which did not permit
censorship of any electronic bulletin boards, either text or graphics, be
restored.
